/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A helper makes a series and stores it in its argument; a second function hands its own argument on to it. Cast inside a rabbit, on a container from outside.

    What a function makes lies in the region it is cast in. A function that hands its parameter to one
    that stores into it stores into it too, so the cast of the outer one is refused. (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O4). */

Bind void to push-into, given (the series of series of number bag):
    Define fresh as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
    Insert fresh into bag.
Done.
Bind void to relay, given (the series of series of number bag):
    Cast push-into on (bag).
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast relay on (keeper).
Done.
State keeper.
